The finding this commit's message records is the one worth keeping: the
reconciliation doc priced the persona split at "more records," but a
certificate has one issuer and issue() requires the provider's master key to
equal it, so per-persona certificates need per-persona signing identities.
The consequence is that a verifier's trusted root set becomes one TrustedRoot
per persona rather than one master key. That is architectural and lands in M5.

No history surgery was done to repair this. An amend was attempted and hit
the wrong commit, because another agent had committed in between; that was
reverted by restoring their message verbatim from the reflog, and this note
is the correct repair for a message that has commits on top of it.
